          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Roller marks on a ceiling come from a few specific causes: dry edges leave lap marks, dry rollers and hard pressure leave edge lines, unprimed patches flash and the wrong nap leaves heavy stipple. Identify the type, fix the cause, then recoat whole sections with a fully loaded roller and a wet edge.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best prevention is a flat paint made for ceilings, good prep and a steady rhythm. Our <a href="/best-ceiling-paint/">ceiling paint picks</a> cover the products that level and hide best.
